# Context

## Why This Way
Remote names here are inverted from convention: origin is upstream
(tobi/walgit) and fork is our fork (nibzard/walgit). The banner and
CLAUDE.md exist so every agent and human sees the one-way flow before
touching anything. CLAUDE.md is just "@AGENTS.md" because Claude Code
loads CLAUDE.md while Codex loads AGENTS.md.

## Gotchas
- The pushurl=no-push guard on origin is LOCAL git config only. It is
  not in this commit, so a fresh clone does not have it. Re-apply with:
  git remote set-url --push origin no-push
- Renaming the remotes was considered and rejected: it would break
  muscle memory and the merge plan assumes current names.

## Related
- Upstream merges follow the 12-batch plan at
  /home/agent/merge-plan-walgit.md (local machine).
